    "q-12797": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12797",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find $b$ if ${b}^{2}-15=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the ${b}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}-15 & =4 \\\\ {b}^{2} & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{b}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{19} \\\\ |b| & =\\sqrt{19} \\\\ b & =\\pm \\sqrt{19}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-12797-a",
