    "q-218607": {
      "dom_id": "step-q218607",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Solve the equation $\\frac{{a}^{2}-5}{3}=0.$ Express your final answer in its simplest form.\n\n$a=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the ${a}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}^{2}-5}{3} & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-5 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ a & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
